@page "/pessoal"
@model PessoalModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = UiText.PersonalTab;
}
<h1>@UiText.PersonalTab</h1>

@*
    Two lists and not one, and the reason is not tidiness.

    An idea can be in both, because a person may vote on an idea of their own. The stronger
    reason is the first day: this page can be empty in two different ways, and on the day
    the board opens everybody is in both at once. One list could only say "empty", and the
    two sentences below could not be told apart even by somebody who wanted to.

    There is no search here. The search narrows the board, and these two lists are already
    narrowed to one person.
*@
<section class="area-pessoal">
    <h2>@UiText.MyIdeasHeading</h2>

    @if (Model.HasSubmittedNothing)
    {
        <div class="estado-vazio">
            <p>@UiText.NoIdeasSubmitted</p>
            <a class="botao botao-principal botao-grande" asp-page="/Nova">@UiText.SubmitIdeaButton</a>
        </div>
    }
    else
    {
        <partial name="_IdeaList" model="@(new IdeaListView { Items = Model.MyIdeas })" />
    }
</section>

<section class="area-pessoal">
    <h2>@UiText.SupportedIdeasHeading</h2>

    @if (Model.HasVotedOnNothing)
    {
        <div class="estado-vazio">
            <p>@UiText.NoIdeasSupported</p>
        </div>
    }
    else
    {
        <partial name="_IdeaList" model="@(new IdeaListView { Items = Model.VotedIdeas })" />
    }
</section>
